# Each layer's nameplate. One row per (filing, layer) that states what the supply can do, as a
# three-point claim. A layer whose nameplate is a typed blank has no row.
#
# Divisibility is two separate questions
#   This relation carries both, because a supply can arrive in whole units and be available only
#   part of the time, at once.
#     `lumpy` + `quantum_*`   the supply arrives in whole units of that size.
#     `window_*`              the supply is only available for that much of a period.
#
# `lumpy` has three states
#   `lumpy` is nullable, and the third state is the point: neither lumpy nor continuous, because
#   nobody said which. A boolean has two states and this question has three.
#
# A derived amount is read worked out
#   As in layers/demand.sqlc, an amount filed `derived` is the figure its fusion works out, and
#   `n_derived` says so. The quantum, the window and the rest are the layer's own, as filed.
#
# Two arms of its own, rather than a restriction
#   layers/demand.sqlc and layers/drawn.sqlc are composition/resolved_quantities.sqlc kept to one
#   quantity. This relation carries the nameplate's own divisibility and window beside the amount,
#   and joining those columns to the resolved figure puts the worked-out arm one plan level deeper
#   under every rule, one more than the deepest statements in the tree can be read back with at
#   compile time. So the amount is stated or worked out in two arms here, the same two arms that
#   relation has, kept to the nameplate.
#
# A blank window is not an empty one
#   There are only two of them. `notApplicable`: the unit has no period, so "five days of what?"
#   has no answer. `unmeasured`: nobody asked, and that is the state in which a time slack cannot
#   be worked out from a clearance.
-- pm:Layer/pm:Nameplate, its Divisibility and its window, with the amount from
-- composition/derived_quantities.sqlc where it is filed `derived`.
SELECT n.filing, n.layer,
       n.amount_low  AS n_low,
       n.amount_mode AS n_mode,
       n.amount_high AS n_high,
       n.amount_unit AS n_unit,
       false AS n_derived,
       n.amount_origin, n.amount_origin_absent,
       n.lumpy, n.divisibility_absent,
       n.quantum_low, n.quantum_mode, n.quantum_high, n.quantum_unit, n.quantum_absent,
       n.window_low, n.window_mode, n.window_high, n.window_unit, n.window_size_absent,
       n.window_absent
FROM pm.nameplate n
WHERE n.amount_low IS NOT NULL
UNION ALL
SELECT n.filing, n.layer, q.low, q.mode, q.high, q.unit, true,
       n.amount_origin, n.amount_origin_absent,
       n.lumpy, n.divisibility_absent,
       n.quantum_low, n.quantum_mode, n.quantum_high, n.quantum_unit, n.quantum_absent,
       n.window_low, n.window_mode, n.window_high, n.window_unit, n.window_size_absent,
       n.window_absent
FROM pm.nameplate n
JOIN (
    :compose(composition/derived_quantities.sqlc)
) q ON q.filing = n.filing AND q.layer = n.layer AND q.quantity = 'nameplate'
WHERE q.low IS NOT NULL
